NNAAMMEE
     aammddssbbwwdd — device driver for the AMD southbridge watchdog timers

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee aammddssbbwwdd

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           amdsbwd_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aammddssbbwwdd driver provides watchdog(4) support for the watchdog timers
     present on the supported chipsets.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The aammddssbbwwdd driver supports the following chipsets:

     ••   AMD SB600/7x0/8x0/9x0 southbridges
     ••   AMD Axx/Hudson/Bolton FCHs
     ••   AMD FCHs integrated into Family 15h Models 60h-6Fh, 70h-7Fh Proces‐
         sors
     ••   AMD FCHs integrated into Family 16h Models 00h-0Fh, 30h-3Fh Proces‐
         sors

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     watchdog(4), watchdog(8), watchdogd(8), watchdog(9)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aammddssbbwwdd driver first appeared in FreeBSD 7.3 and FreeBSD 8.1.

